---
import BaseLayout from '../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const locale = 'en';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="HR & Payroll — Employee Management, Leave, Payroll Processing"
  description="Employee records, leave management, attendance tracking, payroll processing with NSSF and PAYE compliance, appraisals, KPI tracking, and recruitment. Part of Kraal Code ERP."
  locale={locale}
  canonicalUrl="https://kraalcode.com/en/capabilities/hr-payroll/"
>
  <section class="page-hero section--warm">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/en/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/en/capabilities/">Capabilities</a></li><li aria-current="page">HR & Payroll</li></ol></nav>
      <h1>HR & Payroll</h1>
      <p class="page-hero-subtext">From recruitment to retirement. Employee records, leave, attendance, payroll, appraisals, and statutory compliance — in one governed system.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container container--narrow">
    <h2>Who this is for</h2>
    <p>HR managers, payroll officers, department heads, and business owners who need to manage people operations cleanly — contracts, leave, attendance, payroll, and statutory compliance — without maintaining parallel spreadsheets.</p>
    <p>If your organisation pays staff, tracks leave, runs appraisals, or reports to NSSF and URA — and you need those records to flow into the general ledger without manual re-entry — this module handles the full employee lifecycle.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section section--warm"><div class="container">
    <h2>What you can do</h2>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Employee Records</h3><p>Maintain a complete employee master: personal details, contract terms, department, grade, reporting line, bank details, and emergency contacts. Track contract history and renewal dates.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Leave Management</h3><p>Define leave types (annual, sick, maternity, study, unpaid). Employees submit leave requests. Supervisors approve or reject. Leave balances update automatically. Generate leave reports by department or period.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Attendance Tracking</h3><p>Import attendance data from biometric systems. Track daily attendance, overtime, and absences. Generate attendance reports for payroll processing.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Payroll Processing</h3><p>Configure earnings (basic, allowances, overtime) and deductions (NSSF, PAYE, loans, advances). Run monthly payroll with gross-to-net calculations. Generate payslips, bank transfer files, and payment reports.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Statutory Compliance</h3><p>Uganda NSSF and PAYE calculations built in. Configurable for other East African tax authorities. Generate NSSF schedules and PAYE returns in the formats required by authorities.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Performance Appraisals</h3><p>Define appraisal templates with KPIs and competencies. Employees self-assess. Supervisors score and comment. Track appraisal cycles by department and fiscal year.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Organisation Chart</h3><p>Visualise the organisation structure. Show departments, reporting lines, and headcounts. Navigate from the org chart to individual staff profiles.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Recruitment</h3><p>Post positions, receive applications, track candidates through screening and interview stages. Convert successful candidates to employees. Maintain a recruitment pipeline with stage analytics.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container container--narrow">
    <h2>How it connects</h2>
    <p>Payroll is one of the largest cost items in any organisation. This module posts to accounting automatically on approval:</p>
    <ul class="connection-list">
      <li><strong>Accounting</strong> → payroll entries (salary, NSSF, PAYE, net pay) posted to GL on approval</li>
      <li><strong>Manufacturing</strong> → worker assignments and labour cost allocation to production orders</li>
      <li><strong>Projects</strong> → resource allocation and timesheet tracking for project costing</li>
      <li><strong>Self-Service Portal</strong> → employees view payslips, submit leave requests, update profile</li>
    </ul>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section section--warm"><div class="container container--narrow">
    <h2>Controls and permissions</h2>
    <div class="controls-grid">
      <div class="control-item"><h3>Payroll Approval</h3><p>Payroll runs require HR manager approval before posting. Finance reviews and approves the payroll journal. Dual sign-off before funds are released.</p></div>
      <div class="control-item"><h3>Salary Confidentiality</h3><p>Salary details visible only to HR and finance roles. Managers see their team's attendance and leave but not compensation. Self-service shows own payslip only.</p></div>
      <div class="control-item"><h3>Leave Override Control</h3><p>Leave balances cannot be manually adjusted without documented approval. Negative leave balances require director-level authorisation. All adjustments are audited.</p></div>
      <div class="control-item"><h3>Audit Trail</h3><p>Every payroll run, leave approval, appraisal submission, and employee record change is logged with user, timestamp, and IP. INSERT-only log. No HR record can be silently altered.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container">
    <h2>See it in action</h2>
    <p class="screenshot-intro">Screenshots from the live Kraal Code system — coming soon.</p>
    <div class="screenshot-grid">
      <div class="screenshot-slot"><div class="screenshot-placeholder"><span class="screenshot-label">Payroll Run</span><span class="screenshot-note">Live product screenshot — coming soon</span></div></div>
      <div class="screenshot-slot"><div class="screenshot-placeholder"><span class="screenshot-label">Staff Profile</span><span class="screenshot-note">Live product screenshot — coming soon</span></div></div>
      <div class="screenshot-slot"><div class="screenshot-placeholder"><span class="screenshot-label">Leave Calendar</span><span class="screenshot-note">Live product screenshot — coming soon</span></div></div>
      <div class="screenshot-slot"><div class="screenshot-placeholder"><span class="screenshot-label">Performance Appraisal</span><span class="screenshot-note">Live product screenshot — coming soon</span></div></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section--dark section"><div class="container text-center">
    <h2>See HR & Payroll in action</h2>
    <p>Request a demonstration tailored to your people operations needs.</p>
    <a href="/en/contact/" class="btn btn--inverse">Request a Demonstration →</a>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    padding: var(--kc-space-20) 0 var(--kc-space-12);
  }
  .page-hero h1 {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-4xl);
    max-width: 700px;
  }
  .page-hero-subtext {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-lg);
    color: var(--kc-text-secondary);
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin-top: var(--kc-space-4);
  }
  .breadcrumb ol {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--kc-space-2);
    font-size: var(--kc-text-sm);
    color: var(--kc-text-tertiary);
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-6);
  }
  .breadcrumb a {
    color: var(--kc-teal);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .breadcrumb li:not(:last-child)::after {
    content: '/';
    margin-left: var(--kc-space-2);
    color: var(--kc-text-tertiary);
  }
  .container--narrow {
    max-width: var(--kc-container-narrow);
  }
  .container--narrow p {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-base);
    color: var(--kc-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--kc-leading-relaxed);
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-4);
  }
  .feature-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: var(--kc-space-6);
    margin-top: var(--kc-space-8);
  }
  .feature-card {
    padding: var(--kc-space-6);
    background: var(--kc-surface-light);
    border: 1px solid var(--kc-border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--kc-radius-lg);
  }
  .feature-card h3 {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-lg);
    font-family: var(--kc-font-body);
    font-weight: var(--kc-weight-semibold);
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-2);
  }
  .feature-card p {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-sm);
    color: var(--kc-text-secondary);
  }
  .connection-list {
    margin-top: var(--kc-space-4);
  }
  .connection-list li {
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-3);
    font-size: var(--kc-text-base);
    color: var(--kc-text-secondary);
  }
  .connection-list strong {
    color: var(--kc-text-primary);
  }
  .controls-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: var(--kc-space-6);
    margin-top: var(--kc-space-6);
  }
  .control-item {
    padding: var(--kc-space-5);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--kc-teal);
  }
  .control-item h3 {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-base);
    font-family: var(--kc-font-body);
    font-weight: var(--kc-weight-semibold);
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-1);
  }
  .control-item p {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-sm);
    color: var(--kc-text-secondary);
  }
  .screenshot-intro {
    color: var(--kc-text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-6);
  }
  .screenshot-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: var(--kc-space-6);
  }
  .screenshot-placeholder {
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 10;
    background: var(--kc-surface-warm);
    border: 2px dashed var(--kc-border);
    border-radius: var(--kc-radius-lg);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: var(--kc-space-2);
  }
  .screenshot-label {
    font-weight: var(--kc-weight-semibold);
    color: var(--kc-text-primary);
  }
  .screenshot-note {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-sm);
    color: var(--kc-text-tertiary);
  }
  .btn--inverse {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: var(--kc-space-4) var(--kc-space-8);
    font-weight: var(--kc-weight-semibold);
    font-size: var(--kc-text-base);
    border-radius: var(--kc-radius-lg);
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--kc-text-inverse);
    border: 2px solid var(--kc-teal-light);
    transition: all var(--kc-transition-fast);
    text-decoration: none;
    margin-top: var(--kc-space-6);
  }
  .btn--inverse:hover {
    background: var(--kc-teal);
    border-color: var(--kc-teal);
  }
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .page-hero h1 {
      font-size: var(--kc-text-3xl);
    }
    .feature-grid,
    .controls-grid,
    .screenshot-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
